e \\((x_n, y_n) \\to (x_0, y_0)\\) with \\(x_n \\neq y_n\\), the quotient \\(\\frac{\\varphi(y_n) - \\varphi(x_n)}{y_n - x_n} = \\varphi\'(\\xi)\\) with \\(\\xi\\) between \\(x_n\\) and \\(y_n\\) converges to \\(\\varphi\'(x_0)\\) because \\(\\xi \\to x_0\\) and \\(\\varphi\'\\) is continuous. Thus, \\(f\\) is continuous everywhere.\n\n\\boxed{\\mathbb{R}^2}<|im_end|>'], label: \mathbb{R}^2, reward: 1
